Q:
Find the following limit using forms: lim as x -> infinity of e^(-x)/x^2

A:
0

e^(-x)/x^2 = 1/(e^x · x^2). Both e^x -> infinity and x^2 -> infinity. Thus e^x · x^2 -> infinity and form is 1/infinity which approaches 0.

